&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2019 and headquartered in San Francisco, Hightouch enables marketing teams to analyze performance, brainstorm ideas, and generate creative at a speed and quality that wasn&#39;t previously possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Named a Leader in the 2026 Gartner® Magic Quadrant™ for Customer Data Platforms, Hightouch is trusted by leading enterprises like Domino&#39;s, Spotify, Aritzia, Cars.com, Ramp, and PetSmart.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Hightouch, our mission is to help our customers leverage data and AI to grow their businesses. The team is ambitious, impact-driven, efficient — and we believe humility, kindness, and compassion are essential to our success. If you&#39;re energized by velocity, obsessed with raising the bar, and want to build alongside people who care deeply about each other and our customers, we&#39;d love to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring an Executive Assistant to be a force multiplier for our sales leaders and the operating engine behind how the revenue org runs. This is a hands-on role for someone who owns problems end-to-end — from QBR logistics across the org to the weekly follow-through that keeps three growing sales orgs moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hightouch&#39;s revenue team is scaling fast. You&#39;ll be part of the team that makes the whole rhythm run, reporting to the CRO&#39;s Chief of Staff and partnering closely with multiple sales leaders. This is not a role for someone who waits to be handed a schedule. It&#39;s for someone who sees what needs to happen next and makes it happen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Quarterly Business Reviews and offsite logistics end-to-end.&lt;/strong&gt; Plan and run multiple QBRs and team offsites across the org — venues, travel, hotels, catering, evening activities, day-of run-of-show, and materials. Leaders should walk in prepared and walk out with everything handled. You&#39;re the single source of truth for the program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run the operating rhythm of three sales orgs.&lt;/strong&gt; Consolidate agendas, coordinate guest presenters, track takeaways, and ensure follow-up for recurring meetings — including team meetings, forecast/pipeline calls, enablement series, and local leadership meetings. Make sure decisions made in the room actually reach the teams and get done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn meeting notes into finished follow-through.&lt;/strong&gt; Convert 1:1 and forecast-call outputs into tracked next steps and drive them to close. Fire off the Slacks, chase the loose ends, and make sure nothing falls through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear the drag so leaders can lead.&lt;/strong&gt; Protect calendars, triage where it counts, own expenses, and handle meeting logistics. The goal is simple: leaders spend their time selling and building, not coordinating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Plus: You can build the things leaders never have time to build.&lt;/strong&gt; Turn a 30-minute brain-dump into a tangible artifact. Draft AE-sourced outreach for a leader to review and send. Help run an OKR accountability cadence that keeps goals front and center each quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You run complex logistics without dropping a thread.&lt;/strong&gt; Multiple events on overlapping timelines don&#39;t rattle you — you&#39;ve built the tracker, booked the venues, and thought through the day-of before anyone has to ask.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You close loops.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;d rather chase something to done than wait to be reminded. Follow-through is your default, not your exception.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You write like an operator.&lt;/strong&gt; You can draft an agenda, a briefing, or outreach in a leader&#39;s voice and get it 90% of the way there on the first pass.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ve operated in a high-velocity environment.&lt;/strong&gt; Ideally you&#39;ve supported senior leaders or run programs in a fast-growing sales, GTM, or startup setting, and you know how quickly priorities shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re trusted with sensitive information.&lt;/strong&gt; Calendars, comp, recruiting, and deal details pass through you, and discretion is second nature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re fluent in the modern GTM stack — and getting faster with AI.&lt;/strong&gt; Slack, calendar and inbox tooling, CRM, and meeting-notes tools are second nature, and you use AI to move quicker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The salary range for this position is&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;$130,000-$170,000 USD &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;2&quot;&gt;per year, which is location-independent. We also offer meaningful equity compensation in the form of ISO options and offer early exercise and a 10 year post-termination exercise window.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;E-Verify Statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Hightouch participates in E-Verify. After you join the team, we&#39;ll verify your eligibility to work in the U.S. by submitting information from your Form I-9 to the Social Security Administration and, if needed, the Department of Homeland Security. This process happens post-hire only — we never use E-Verify to pre-screen applicants.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
