&lt;li&gt;Externally evangelize Hightouch at field events, customer engagements, and webinars&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-6 years in competitive intelligence, product marketing, or market research, ideally in B2B SaaS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong primary and secondary research skills (win/loss interviews, analyst reports, public filings, review sites, pricing pages); ability to synthesize messy, conflicting signals into a clear point of view; comfortable building and maintaining structured frameworks (battlecards, comparison matrices, positioning maps).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of producing content that sales and marketing actually use — battlecards, competitive decks, objection handling guides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Storytelling: Proficient in turning complex, technology-heavy topics into digestible, compelling stories that resonate with target audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication Skills: Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for crafting clear, persuasive messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional fluency: has worked closely with sales (win/loss, deal support), product (roadmap and positioning input), and marketing (messaging, launches); understands sales cycles well enough to know what reps need in the moment, not just what&#39;s &quot;interesting.&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain fit: familiarity with data infrastructure, CDPs, MarTech, or adjacent technical B2B markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership: flags competitive shifts before sales asks, not just after losing a deal; comfortable being the first person to build this function rather than inheriting an existing playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
